---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Send JSON-RPC calls and batches, and fetch OpenRPC catalogs

Usage: rustman rpc [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  call      Send one JSON-RPC call (an endpoint with a method, or a request file) and print its result or error object
  batch     Send calls from a JSON array, a YAML list or JSON lines as one batch (100 calls per batch) and print the results in input order
  discover  Fetch an endpoint's OpenRPC document with rpc.discover and cache it
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman rpc call http://127.0.0.1:8332 getblockcount --header "Authorization: Basic {{btc_auth}}"
  rustman rpc call {{rpc_url}} eth_getBalance '["0xabc...", "latest"]'
  rustman rpc call wss://node.example eth_subscribe '["newHeads"]' --subscribe eth_subscription --unsubscribe eth_unsubscribe
  rustman rpc call requests/chain/head.rman.yaml
  printf '{"method":"eth_chainId"}\n' | rustman rpc batch {{rpc_url}} -
  rustman rpc discover {{rpc_url}}
